# port-patches.sh: glm/pub-r5-on-186 @ 1305bda37155 over glm/zig-engine-fixes-on-186 @ e027c49cd06d (commits ff464227b3d5..3a03212607f6); regenerate with scripts/port-patches.sh, do not edit
core/spill: the disk block store of spill v2 (port of GLM 0110's store, lifted from the DeepSeek port)

Spill v2's family-neutral, GPU-free store, the DeepSeek port's core/spill/ as
it stands on that port's engine, lifted onto v1.0.7 (whose direct_io has the
same API): kept states in 2,048-token blocks that turns and forks of a
conversation share (the id chain salted with the lineage names them, so a
later turn writes only its own blocks), small per-point sections, writes
staged through the write-at-keep ring (a kill keeps only fully published
points), recovery at open, reads through read slots with all-rank presence and
validation, and room made by conversation (issue #122) under a cap, a disk
floor, a quota and a turn bound.

- The namespace prefix is the family's (Config.prefix; GLM's is glm-spill-),
  and open prunes only that family's other builds, names of exactly
  <prefix><16 hex>, so GLM and DeepSeek can share one spill folder.
- Kept although GLM uses only the first (with KV sharding) and not yet the
  second: owner-sharded layouts (a part-salted lineage, a foreign part's
  block size) and picture points (manifest version 3); a text point is
  written as version 2.

Switch: none (a library). Nothing calls it before the GLM tier (the spill
blocks patch): with no store opened nothing changes, and Zig's lazy analysis
leaves it out of the server binary. Tests: the DeepSeek store's tests (format,
recovery, crash points, lineage, eviction, concurrent reads) plus a GLM-shaped
check of grid turns, the family prune and prefix refusals; its mutants are
caught.

Measured on the pair: under the GLM tier in round 2's image (g2; the spill
blocks patch says what).

Credits: Robert Wojciechowski (GitHub @wojo, X @rwojo); spill v2's block store
design (2,048-token blocks, lineage, the write-at-keep ring, release and fsync
order): BadAd84 (https://github.com/BadAd84),
MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold#118; GLM patches 0088
and 0110, MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold#78 and #124.

Tests on a file system that has O_DIRECT (ext4 on the Sparks' disks): the scripted short writes (fsio.zig's Script, store_test.zig's
hook) used to issue a real partial pwrite on an O_DIRECT descriptor, which ext4 refuses with EINVAL, so "a partial
direct write off the 4 KiB grid finishes buffered" and the store test's "write faults" check failed unless the temp
directory was tmpfs. fsio.pwritePartial makes that one write buffered and puts the descriptor back; the product
write path is unchanged.
Apply from the checkout root with: git apply 0018-zig-core-spill-store.patch

